/**
 * @component banner
 * @summary A styled container for display of important information with two size variants and color themes.
 * @remarks Banners present key information with a heading and content in a contained block. Use `-size-compact` for minimal spacing and `-size-relaxed` for expanded spacing. Apply a color theme with `-theme-sea` or `-theme-violet` to change the background and icon colors. Close buttons and icons can be positioned within the banner structure.
 * @selector .PFX-banner
 * @modifier -size-compact — Compact sizing with smaller heading, content font size, and tighter spacing.
 * @modifier -size-relaxed — Relaxed sizing (default) with larger heading, content font size, and expanded spacing.
 * @modifier -theme-sea — Sea/teal color theme.
 * @modifier -theme-violet — Violet color theme.
 * @part .heading — The banner heading.
 * @part .content — The banner content area.
 * @part .icon — Optional leading icon or image container.
 * @part .close-button — Optional close/dismiss button.
 * @accessibility Use semantically appropriate heading elements (h1-h6) for `.heading`. Ensure sufficient color contrast between text and background. For dismissible banners, provide an accessible close button with `aria-label`.
 * @example -canvas-rce -docs
 * ```html
 * <div class="PFX-banner -size-relaxed -theme-sea">
 *   <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
 *   <div class="heading">Important Information</div>
 *   <div class="content">This is an important message that needs your attention.</div>
 *   <button class="close-button" aria-label="Close banner"></button>
 * </div>
 * ```
 * @example -docs
 * ```html
 * <div class="PFX-banner -size-compact -theme-sea">
 *   <div class="heading">Compact Banner</div>
 *   <div class="content">This banner uses compact sizing.</div>
 * </div>
 * <div class="PFX-banner -size-relaxed -theme-violet">
 *   <div class="heading">Relaxed Banner</div>
 *   <div class="content">This banner uses relaxed sizing.</div>
 * </div>
 * ```
 */
.PFX-banner {
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--instui-component-banner-font-family);
