/**
 * @component global-nav-bar
 * @selector .pfx-global-nav-bar
 * @summary A vertical navigation rail of icon-over-label items, with a minimized icons-only mode.
 * @remarks Sets its own `gap` between nav items and its own `padding`; chaining a `-gap-*`/`-p-*`/`-padding-*` spacing utility modifier overrides those built-in values. See the `global-nav-bar.item` member for the individual nav entries.
 * @modifier -minimized — Collapse to icons only (labels hidden). @affects global-nav-bar.item — Hides the item's label.
 * @modifier -icon-* — Render a glyph icon in each nav item.
 * @part .label — The nav item's text label.
 * @a11y Label the `<nav>` with aria-label so it's announced as a named navigation landmark.
 * @structure
 * .pfx-global-nav-bar {
 *   .item:one-or-more {}
 * }
 * @example -canvas-rce -docs
 * ```html
 * <nav class="pfx-global-nav-bar" aria-label="Primary">
 *   <a class="item -selected" href="#">
 *     <span class="pfx-icon -icon-house"></span>
 *     <span class="label">Home</span>
 *   </a>
 *   <a class="item" href="#">
 *     <span class="pfx-icon -icon-inbox"></span>
 *     <span class="label">Inbox</span>
 *   </a>
 *   <a class="item" href="#">
 *     <span class="pfx-icon -icon-calendar"></span>
 *     <span class="label">Calendar</span>
 *   </a>
 *   <a class="item" href="#">
 *     <span class="pfx-icon -icon-settings"></span>
 *     <span class="label">Settings</span>
 *   </a>
 * </nav>
 * ```
 * @example -automatica11y
 * ```html
 * <nav class="pfx-global-nav-bar" aria-label="Primary">
 *   <a class="item -selected" href="#home" aria-current="page">
 *     <span class="-icon-house" aria-hidden="true"></span>
 *     <span class="label">Home</span>
 *   </a>
 *   <a class="item" href="#inbox">
